                {
                  "id": "h-sizes",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Common Dry Van Sizes and Capacities",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "sizes"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-sizes-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "When comparing dry van sizes, most trailers fall into a few standard categories.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "cards-sizes-2",
                  "type": "card-lists",
                  "props": {
                    "variant": "type3",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "title": "53-Foot Dry Van",
                        "points": [
                          {
                            "text": "Interior length: ~53 feet"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Interior width: ~102 inches"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Interior height: ~110 inches"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Payload capacity: ~45,000–48,000 lbs"
                          }
                        ],
                        "intro": "The most common option in North America."
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "48-Foot Dry Van",
                        "points": [
                          {
                            "text": "Easier maneuverability"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Lower empty weight"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Good capacity for regional routes"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Payload: ~46,000–50,000 lbs"
                          }
                        ],
                        "intro": "Slightly smaller but still widely used."
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Lightweight Dry Van",
                        "points": [
                          {
                            "text": "Aluminum components"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Composite panels"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Reinforced flooring systems"
                          }
                        ],
                        "intro": "Designed to maximize payload by reducing utility weight."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-sizes-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Because of its balance between space and efficiency, the 53-foot model is often the preferred choice for long-haul freight. A lighter trailer can allow operators to haul additional freight without exceeding weight limits.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
