                {
                  "id": "h-factors",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Factors That Affect Semi Trailer Capacity",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "factors"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-factors-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Even if two trailers are the same length, their semi trailer capacity can vary significantly. Several factors influence how much cargo a trailer can carry.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h3-factors-2",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "1. Trailer Construction",
                    "headingLevel": 3,
                    "align": "left"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-factors-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "The materials used in a trailer directly impact its empty weight. Common construction options include steel frame trailers, aluminum frame trailers, and composite wall designs. Lightweight construction often increases payload capacity while maintaining durability.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h3-factors-4",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "2. Flooring Strength",
                    "headingLevel": 3,
                    "align": "left"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-factors-5",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Freight type matters. High-strength flooring systems are designed to handle beverage loads and industrial equipment. A reinforced floor may increase durability but slightly increase overall weight.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h3-factors-6",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "3. Freight Type",
                    "headingLevel": 3,
                    "align": "left"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-factors-7",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Different freight types affect how payload capacity is used, including consumer goods, retail products, food distribution, and manufacturing components. The goal is maximizing load efficiency without exceeding weight limits.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-compared",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Dry Vans Compared to Other Types of Trailers for Trucks",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "compared"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-compared-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Dry vans are one of the most widely used types of trailers for trucks, but they aren't the only option. Understanding the differences helps operators choose the right equipment.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "cards-compared-2",
                  "type": "card-lists",
                  "props": {
                    "variant": "type3",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "title": "Dry Van Trailers",
                        "points": [
                          {
                            "text": "Weather protection"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Secure cargo transport"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Versatile freight compatibility"
                          }
                        ],
                        "intro": "Best for enclosed freight such as retail products, electronics, or packaged goods."
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Refrigerated (Reefer)",
                        "points": [
                          {
                            "text": "Food distribution"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Perishable goods"
                          }
                        ],
                        "intro": "Designed for temperature-controlled cargo."
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Flatbed Trailers",
                        "points": [
                          {
                            "text": "Construction materials"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Machinery"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Industrial equipment"
                          }
                        ],
                        "intro": "Ideal for oversized freight."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-compared-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "For many operators, dry vans remain the most versatile and cost-effective trailer option.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
